 ## Background
-The method originates from the work on Interactive Isosurface Ray Tracing of Large Octree Volumes by Wald et al. (2006) [S2, S3][S5, unofficial]. It was developed to efficiently traverse large octree structures for isosurface rendering, leveraging the hierarchical nature of the octree to skip empty space. The approach was further refined and applied in various contexts, including rendering piecewise approximations of SDFs [S1] and implicit surface ray tracing [S5, unofficial]. The duality between voxels and cells, mapping voxels to the lower-left corner of a cell, was also observed in this context [S4, unofficial].
